#!/usr/bin/env xetal
# HEX1000 counting on its outputs: three instructions in a loop, run
# for 12 instructions. First the program as it sits in the ROM, in the
# order it runs: PC steps 0, 1, 3 (the shift register's order, which
# the assembler follows), so the third instruction is at address 3.
# Then the registers after reset and after each instruction: A counts
# at IA, BR takes PC back to 0 (S is 1, so it is always taken), and O
# is A and S (bit 4, so 16 + A) as TDO left it, one IA behind.
# Run with "just demo-lib Hex1000 counter".
"hx:" u_se< "Hex1000"
rom := hx:a_ssemble "loop: TDO   ; A and S to the outputs\nIA          ; count\nBR loop     ; S is 1: always taken"
0 hx:l_isting rom
hx:RegNames hx:t_able rom hx:t_race (hx:Reset, 0, 12)
